3) Deterministic gcd-reduction transport (non-coprime tube → reduced coprime tube)

Since TubeData requires Nat.Coprime a.natAbs q.natAbs, you cannot even build td until you reduce. The transport lemma you need should live at the BG tube level (no coprime assumptions).

Let P : BGTube.Params, a : ℤ, q : ℕ, s : ℤ. Define

g : ℕ := Nat.gcd a.natAbs q

q0 : ℕ := q / g

a0 : ℤ := a / (g : ℤ) (valid because g ∣ a.natAbs, hence g ∣ a)

U0 : ℕ := (P.U + g - 1) / g (ceiling of U/g, enough for transport)

s0 : ℤ := s / (g : ℤ) (you can incorporate s % g into the + (g-1) padding as above)

Then prove:

theorem tubeFinset_subset_gcdReduced
    (P : BGTube.Params) (a : ℤ) (q : ℕ) (s : ℤ) :
    let g : ℕ := Nat.gcd a.natAbs q
    let q0 : ℕ := q / g
    let a0 : ℤ := a / (g : ℤ)
    let s0 : ℤ := s / (g : ℤ)
    let U0 : ℕ := (P.U + g - 1) / g
    BGTube.tubeFinset P a q s ⊆ BGTube.tubeFinset ({P with U := U0}) a0 q0 s0 := by
  -- use `mem_tubeFinset_iff` and the arithmetic identity
  --   shear a q s p = (g:ℤ) * shear a0 q0 s0 p - (s % g)
  -- then `|g*t - r| ≤ U` ⇒ `|t| ≤ ceil((U + g - 1)/g)`.
  ...

And then your support transfer is immediate:

theorem support_transfer
    {F : TubePoint → ℂ}
    (hF : ∀ p, F p ≠ 0 → p ∈ BGTube.tubeFinset P a q s) :
    ∀ p, F p ≠ 0 → p ∈ BGTube.tubeFinset ({P with U := U0}) a0 q0 s0 :=
by
  intro p hp
  exact (tubeFinset_subset_gcdReduced P a q s) (hF p hp)

